---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About — Dhyai"
  description="DHYAI develops composed surfaces through drawing, material testing, and measured hand printing. Each study is released as a complete object."
  ogImage="/assets/images/studio_glimpse_detail.jpg"
  ogUrl="/about.html"
  currentPage="about"
>

  <!-- ══ Page hero ══ -->
  <div class="page-hero">
    <img
      src="/assets/images/studio_glimpse_detail.jpg"
      alt="Dhyai studio"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
    >
    <div class="page-hero-overlay"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- ══ About intro ══ -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <span class="kicker" style="margin-bottom:1.2rem">The Studio</span>
    <div class="rule-h"></div>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,5rem); letter-spacing:.2em; margin-bottom:2rem">About</h1>
    <div style="max-width:600px">
      <p style="margin-bottom:1.2rem">
        DHYAI develops composed surfaces shaped by proportion and measured repetition.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1.2rem">
        Each study progresses through drawing and material testing until the structure settles.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1.2rem">
        Time is considered within the composition — influencing spacing, density, and rhythm.
        Objects are released as complete studies, available in defined formats.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Studio section ══ -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="two-col reveal">
      <div class="two-col-img">
        <img
          src="/assets/images/material_surface_close.jpg"
          alt="Material surface detail — cotton selected for printing clarity"
          loading="lazy"
        >
      </div>
      <div class="two-col-text">
        <span class="kicker">Material</span>
        <div class="rule-h"></div>
        <h2>Cotton for surface clarity</h2>
        <p>
          Cotton is selected for surface clarity and printing response.
          Weight and weave are matched to each study before production begins.
        </p>
        <p>
          The first Dhyai space operates as a working studio and concept store.
          Studies are developed, printed, and reviewed within the same space they are eventually shown.
          Each surface is assessed in light and material before it is made available.
        </p>
        <a href="/process.html" class="btn-enquire">View the process</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Founder ══ -->
  <section class="section" style="border-top:1px solid rgba(237,227,204,.05)">
    <div class="two-col reverse reveal">
      <div class="two-col-text">
        <span class="kicker">Founder</span>
        <div class="rule-h"></div>
        <h2>An object is a record of decisions</h2>
        <p>
          Every surface at Dhyai is the result of a sustained sequence of choices —
          about proportion, density, and the right moment to stop.
        </p>
        <p>
          The studio was founded to make objects that earn their place slowly.
          Not through novelty, but through clarity.
        </p>
        <p>
          Based in Bengaluru. Made to order.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="two-col-img">
        <img
          src="/assets/images/founder.webp"
          alt="Dhyai founder"
          loading="lazy"
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Values ══ -->
  <section class="section" style="border-top:1px solid rgba(237,227,204,.05); text-align:center">
    <div class="statement reveal">
      <span class="kicker" style="margin-bottom:2rem">Why Dhyai</span>
      <div class="rule" style="margin-bottom:3rem"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3.5vw,2.8rem); letter-spacing:.18em; margin-bottom:2rem">
        A stone from a riverbed sits on the shelf for years.<br>
        It is time embodied in material.
      </h2>
      <p style="max-width:480px; margin:0 auto">
        Dhyai makes objects that are built to stay. Linen that improves with washing.
        Brass that accumulates your handling. Things worth keeping.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
